{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/miamidiagrams\/miamistatemachine\/statemachine\/dotdiagram"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"nonisolated","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dotDiagram","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["dot -Tsvg order.dot -o order.svg"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every state is a node, named by its description. The states connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by transitions are connected by an arrow, labeled with the events. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"several events lead from a state to the same state, they share one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrow. The initial state has an arrow leading to it from a point, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending states are drawn with a double outline.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The diagram is the same every time, whatever order the transitions were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"given in, so it can be compared with a saved diagram. This needs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states to have different descriptions. States with the same description","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are still different nodes, told apart by a number added to their names,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but which of the states that gets which number can differ.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of transitions."}]}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The definition of the state machine as a diagram, in the DOT language"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of Graphviz. Save it to a file, and Graphviz draws the diagram:"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dotDiagram","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:17MiamiStateMachine0bC0C0A8DiagramsE10dotDiagramSSvp","modules":[{"name":"MiamiDiagrams","relatedModules":["MiamiStateMachine"]}],"extendedModule":"MiamiStateMachine","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateMachineEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"title":"dotDiagram"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MiamiDiagrams\/documentation\/MiamiDiagrams\/MiamiStateMachine\/StateMachine\/dotDiag